   $q$Why does the fable end with the moon appearing after everyone is asleep?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To stress that waiting for the bigger helper would have left the beetle lost all night.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To explain that fireflies only glow on nights when the moon is hidden.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"To show that the moon was angry at the fireflies for taking its job.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To prove that the beetle would have found his way home without any help.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To stress that waiting for the bigger helper would have left the beetle lost all night.$q$, $q$The moon arrives too late to matter, which strengthens the lesson that acting now beats waiting. Nothing suggests the beetle could have found home alone, since his calls were growing "softer and more frightened."$q$, 'draft', '825b3092-fb82-5c21-bd93-b8164252b46a')
