   $q$Which statement best expresses the theme of the story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Winning a record is the only way to make a coach proud.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Officials at track meets usually make mistakes when they measure.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"},{"text":"Long jumpers should practice landing so they never fall backward.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Being honest matters more than winning, even when no one would know.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Being honest matters more than winning, even when no one would know.$q$, $q$Rafael reports the handprint that nobody else saw and gives up the record, yet he ends up smiling. His coach is proud of his honesty, not a record, so the third choice contradicts the ending.$q$, 'draft', '5b05a701-5743-55e6-85f7-85d5889a54ef')
