   $q$Which statement best expresses the theme of the story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Solar ovens work best when they are tested on a sunny blacktop.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"},{"text":"Listening to quieter voices can lead to better ideas and better work.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Teams should always let the loudest member make every decision.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Using more materials always makes a science project more successful.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Listening to quieter voices can lead to better ideas and better work.$q$, $q$The oven works only after Amara listens to Joon's idea, and she ends by asking about his notebook. The story shows that more foil did not help, so the second choice is the opposite of what happens.$q$, 'draft', '1c4b0c21-cdcc-54b9-9ab5-b272f28ef127')
