values
  ('0f2d576b-9eac-5fac-bdd7-3b94e4ee0a58', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-theme-summary'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The speaker has the most amazing night ever, and everyone should visit an observatory.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"The speaker climbs a hill in a winter coat and walks back down a frozen path.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"On a winter night at an observatory, the speaker sees countless stars and distant newborn stars, feels small but amazed, and leaves deep in thought.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The speaker becomes frightened by how big space is and wants to go home.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$On a winter night at an observatory, the speaker sees countless stars and distant newborn stars, feels small but amazed, and leaves deep in thought.$q$, $q$The correct summary covers the visit, what the speaker sees and how the speaker feels. The poem says "I felt no fear," so the frightened version contradicts the text.$q$, 'draft', 'f0c7f22a-0c88-5440-a63c-8da729bb5b11')
