   $q$How does the second stanza, where more and more stars appear, help develop the theme?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It explains that the guide turned on brighter lights inside the dome.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows the sky growing bigger to the speaker, which builds the sense of a vast universe.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that the speaker spilled salt on a sheet before the trip.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It shows that the speaker is bored because the stars all look the same.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows the sky growing bigger to the speaker, which builds the sense of a vast universe.$q$, $q$As the speaker's eyes adjust, the stars become "too many to repeat," which grows the feeling of vastness. The salt is a comparison describing the stars, not an event that really happened.$q$, 'draft', 'f0c7f22a-0c88-5440-a63c-8da729bb5b11')
