   $q$How does the rehearsal moment when the first violins play alone help develop the theme?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that Hana's section is not very skilled at playing the melody.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"It shows that Mr. Adeyemi wants to punish the second violins for not listening.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It explains why the audience clapped so loudly after the final piece.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"It lets Lucia hear how empty the music sounds without her section's part.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It lets Lucia hear how empty the music sounds without her section's part.$q$, $q$The melody alone sounds "thin and floaty," then "warm and full" with the harmony, which shows Lucia her part matters. The thin sound comes from missing harmony, not from Hana's section playing badly.$q$, 'draft', 'bd979aea-5281-595d-9d5a-52b19c1e442b')
